.TH LLAPI_FIND 3 2026-07-03 "Lustre User API" "Lustre Library Functions"
.SH NAME
llapi_find, llapi_find_with_cb \- find files in a Lustre filesystem with
extensive filtering capabilities
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <lustre/lustreapi.h>
.PP
.BI "int llapi_find(char *" path ", struct find_param *" param );
.PP
.BI "int llapi_find_with_cb(char *" path ", struct find_param *" param ,
.BI "                       llapi_find_cb_t " cb_init ",
.BI "                       llapi_find_cb_t " cb_fini );
.PP
.BI "typedef int (*llapi_find_cb_t)(char *" path ", int " p ", int *" d ,
.BI "                               struct find_param *" param ,
.BI "                               struct dirent64 *" de );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR llapi_find ()
and
.BR llapi_find_with_cb ()
functions traverse a Lustre filesystem directory tree starting at
.I path
and identify files and directories matching criteria specified in the
.I param
structure. These functions provide programmatic access to file search
capabilities similar to
.BR "lfs find" (1)
command.
.PP
.B llapi_find()
uses default callback functions for file matching and directory processing.
.PP
.B llapi_find_with_cb()
allows custom callback functions to be specified:
.TP
.I cb_init
Callback invoked for each file/directory entry during traversal. If
.BR NULL ,
uses the default
.BR cb_find_init ()
callback.
.TP
.I cb_fini
Callback invoked after processing a directory's contents. If
.BR NULL ,
uses the default
.BR cb_common_fini ()
callback.
.SS Traversal Algorithm
The traversal algorithm varies depending on whether parallel processing
is enabled:
.PP
.B Single-threaded Mode (fp_thread_count == 0 or 1):
.PP
Uses pure depth-first traversal via the internal
.BR llapi_semantic_traverse ()
function. For each directory:
.IP 1. 4
Call
.I cb_init
callback on the directory itself
.IP 2.
Read all directory entries
.IP 3.
For non-directory entries: call
.I cb_init
then
.I cb_fini
.IP 4.
For subdirectories: recursively call
.BR llapi_semantic_traverse ()
.IP 5.
Call
.I cb_fini
callback on the directory
.PP
.B Parallel Mode (fp_thread_count > 1):
.PP
Uses a work-stealing queue architecture with multiple worker threads.
The traversal is
.I not
pure depth-first; instead, subdirectories are added to a shared work queue for
parallel processing:
.IP 1. 4
Main thread initializes a
.B find_work_queue
with the starting path
.IP 2.
.I N
worker threads are created (where
.I N
=
.IR fp_thread_count )
.IP 3.
Each worker thread:
.RS 4
.IP \- 2
Dequeues a work unit (directory) from the queue head
.IP \-
Calls
.BR llapi_semantic_traverse ()
on that directory
.IP \-
During traversal, when a subdirectory is encountered, instead of recursing
immediately, a new work unit is created and added to the queue tail.
.IP \-
Non-directory files are processed immediately
.IP \-
Repeats until queue is empty and all work units complete
.RE
.IP 4.
Main thread waits for
.I fwq_active_units
to reach zero before returning
.PP
This work-stealing design provides load balancing: idle workers automatically
pick up work from the shared queue, and directory trees are processed
in parallel rather than sequentially.
.PP
.B Traversal Control Fields:
.TP
.I fp_max_depth
Maximum directory depth to traverse (0 = no limit).
.TP
.I fp_min_depth
Minimum directory depth before processing entries.
.TP
.I fp_recursive
Enable recursive directory descent (default: enabled).
.TP
.I fp_thread_count
Number of parallel worker threads:
.RS
.IP \- 2
0 or 1: Single-threaded depth-first traversal
.IP \- 2
>1: Parallel traversal with work-stealing queue
.RE
.TP
.I fp_stop_on_error
If set, stop entire traversal on first error. In parallel mode, sets
.I fwq_shutdown
flag to terminate all workers.
.SS Internal Traversal Implementation
Both single-threaded and parallel modes use the internal
.BR llapi_semantic_traverse ()
function as the core traversal engine. This function:
.PP
.B Opens and processes a single directory:
.IP 1. 4
Opens the directory using
.BR open (2)
with
.B O_RDONLY|O_NDELAY|O_DIRECTORY
flags
.IP 2.
Reopens with
.B O_NOFOLLOW
to detect foreign symlink directories
.IP 3.
Calls
.I cb_init
callback on the directory (if provided)
.IP 4.
Converts the file descriptor to
.B DIR*
using
.BR fdopendir (3)
.IP 5.
Iterates through directory entries using
.BR readdir (3)
.PP
.B For each directory entry:
.IP \- 2
Skips "." and ".." entries
.IP \-
Appends entry name to path buffer (with '/' separator)
.IP \-
For
.BR DT_DIR " (directories):"
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
In single-threaded mode: recursively calls
.BR llapi_semantic_traverse ()
.IP \(bu
In parallel mode: calls
.BR work_unit_create_and_add ()
to enqueue for worker threads
.RE
.IP \-
For other entry types: calls
.I cb_init
then
.I cb_fini
callbacks
.IP \-
Removes entry name from path buffer (restores to parent directory)
.PP
.B After processing all entries:
.IP \- 2
Calls
.I cb_fini
callback on the directory itself
.IP \-
Closes directory and file descriptors
.PP
.B Path buffer management:
The path buffer is modified in-place during traversal. The buffer must be sized
at least 2 * PATH_MAX + 1 bytes to accommodate the deepest possible paths.
Entry names are appended with '/' separators during descent and removed during
ascent.
.PP
.B Depth tracking:
The
.I fp_depth
field tracks current depth (0 = root). Before descending into a subdirectory, if
.I fp_depth
==
.IR fp_max_depth ,
the callback returns 1 to skip descent. After incrementing depth, if
.I fp_depth
<
.IR fp_min_depth ,
callbacks are skipped (but traversal continues).
.PP
.B File descriptor optimization:
Uses
.BR openat (2)
when parent directory file descriptor is available, avoiding full path
resolution overhead. Keeps directory file descriptors open during traversal for
efficient subdirectory access.
.SS Work Queue Architecture (Parallel Mode)
When
.I fp_thread_count
> 1, the parallel find uses a
.B find_work_queue
structure to coordinate worker threads:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
struct find_work_queue {
    struct find_work_unit *fwq_head;  /* Dequeue from head */
    struct find_work_unit *fwq_tail;  /* Enqueue to tail */
    pthread_mutex_t fwq_lock;
    pthread_cond_t fwq_sleep_cond;
    atomic_int fwq_active_units;      /* Active work count */
    bool fwq_shutdown;                /* Shutdown flag */
    int fwq_error;                    /* First error code */
    llapi_find_cb_t fwq_cb_init;      /* Init callback */
    llapi_find_cb_t fwq_cb_fini;      /* Fini callback */
};

struct find_work_unit {
    struct find_work_unit *fwu_next;
    struct find_param *fwu_param;     /* Deep copy */
    struct dirent64 *fwu_de;
    char *fwu_path;
};
.EE
.in
.PP
.B Queue Operations:
.TP
.B Enqueue
When
.BR llapi_semantic_traverse ()
encounters a subdirectory (in parallel mode), it calls
.BR work_unit_create_and_add ()
which:
.RS
.IP 1. 4
Creates a work unit with a deep copy of
.I find_param
.IP 2.
Increments
.I fwq_active_units
atomically
.IP 3.
Adds unit to queue tail (under
.IR fwq_lock )
.IP 4.
Signals
.I fwq_sleep_cond
to wake one waiting worker
.RE
.TP
.B Dequeue
Worker threads dequeue from the queue head:
.RS
.IP 1. 4
Acquire
.I fwq_lock
.IP 2.
Wait on
.I fwq_sleep_cond
if queue is empty and not shutting down
.IP 3.
Remove unit from head, update
.I fwq_head
pointer
.IP 4.
Release
.I fwq_lock
.IP 5.
Process the work unit
.IP 6.
Decrement
.I fwq_active_units
atomically
.RE
.TP
.B Work Stealing
Idle workers automatically "steal" work from the shared queue. This provides
dynamic load balancing without requiring work distribution logic.
.TP
.B Completion Detection
Main thread polls
.I fwq_active_units
(using atomic read). When it reaches zero, all subdirectories have been
processed and all workers are idle or waiting.
.TP
.B Error Handling
If any worker encounters an error and
.I fp_stop_on_error
is set:
.RS
.IP \- 2
Worker sets
.I fwq_shutdown
= true
.IP \-
Worker broadcasts
.I fwq_sleep_cond
to wake all workers
.IP \-
All workers exit their processing loops
.IP \-
Main thread detects shutdown and returns error
.RE
.SS Callback Interface
Custom callbacks must conform to the
.B llapi_find_cb_t
signature:
.PP
.EX
int callback(char *path, int p, int *d, struct find_param *param,
             struct dirent64 *de);
.EE
.in
.PP
Parameters:
.TP
.I path
Full path to the current file/directory being processed.
.TP
.I p
File descriptor of the parent directory (-1 if not available).
.TP
.I d
Pointer to file descriptor of current entry (NULL for non-directories).
.TP
.I param
Pointer to the
.B find_param
structure. The
.I fp_cb_data
field can be used to pass custom callback data.
.TP
.I de
Directory entry structure (NULL for the root path).
.PP
Return values from callbacks:
.TP
.B 0
Continue traversal normally.
.TP
.B 1
Skip descending into this directory (for directories only).
.TP
.B -1
Stop traversal completely.
.TP
.B Other
Error code (negative values).
.SS Matching Conditions
The
.B find_param
structure supports extensive matching conditions. All conditions must be
satisfied for a file to match (logical AND). Fields must be initialized to 0
before use, then set as needed:
.PP
.B File Type and Name Matching:
.TP
.I fp_type
File type to match (S_IFREG, S_IFDIR, S_IFLNK, etc.). Set
.I fp_exclude_type
to invert the match.
.TP
.I fp_pattern
Filename pattern using
.BR fnmatch (3)
syntax. Set
.I fp_exclude_pattern
to exclude matching names.
.PP
.B Owner and Permissions:
.TP
.I fp_uid
User ID to match. Set
.I fp_check_uid
to enable and
.I fp_exclude_uid
to invert.
.TP
.I fp_gid
Group ID to match. Set
.I fp_check_gid
to enable and
.I fp_exclude_gid
to invert.
.TP
.I fp_perm
Permission bits to match. Set
.I fp_perm_sign
to one of:
.BR LFS_FIND_PERM_EXACT " (exact match),"
.BR LFS_FIND_PERM_ALL " (all bits set),"
or
.BR LFS_FIND_PERM_ANY " (any bits set)."
Set
.I fp_exclude_perm
to invert.
.TP
.I fp_projid
Project ID to match. Set
.I fp_check_projid
to enable and
.I fp_exclude_projid
to invert.
.PP
.B Time-based Matching:
.TP
.I fp_atime
Access time to compare (seconds since epoch). Set
.I fp_asign
to -1 (older), 0 (exact), or 1 (newer). Set
.I fp_exclude_atime
to invert.
.I fp_time_margin
specifies tolerance in seconds.
.TP
.I fp_mtime
Modification time. Same semantics as
.IR fp_atime .
Use
.I fp_msign
and
.IR fp_exclude_mtime .
.TP
.I fp_ctime
Change time. Same semantics as
.IR fp_atime .
Use
.I fp_csign
and
.IR fp_exclude_ctime .
.TP
.I fp_btime
Birth/creation time. Same semantics as
.IR fp_atime .
Use
.I fp_bsign
and
.IR fp_exclude_btime .
.TP
.I fp_newerxy
Enable
.BR --newerXY
comparison. Uses
.I fp_newery
array for reference times indexed by
.B NEWERXY_ATIME
(0),
.B NEWERXY_MTIME
(1),
.B NEWERXY_CTIME
(2),
.B NEWERXY_BTIME
(3).
.PP
.B Size and Blocks:
.TP
.I fp_size
File size in bytes. Set
.I fp_check_size
to enable,
.I fp_size_sign
to -1/0/1 (smaller/exact/larger), and
.I fp_size_units
for block size units. Set
.I fp_exclude_size
to invert.
.TP
.I fp_blocks
Number of blocks. Set
.I fp_check_blocks
to enable,
.I fp_blocks_sign
to -1/0/1, and
.I fp_blocks_units
for units. Set
.I fp_exclude_blocks
to invert.
.PP
.B Lustre-specific Attributes:
.TP
.I fp_stripe_size
Stripe size in bytes. Set
.I fp_check_stripe_size
to enable,
.I fp_stripe_size_sign
to -1/0/1, and
.I fp_stripe_size_units
for units. Set
.I fp_exclude_stripe_size
to invert.
.TP
.I fp_stripe_count
Number of stripes. Set
.I fp_check_stripe_count
to enable,
.I fp_stripe_count_sign
to -1/0/1. Set
.I fp_exclude_stripe_count
to invert.
.TP
.I fp_poolname
OST pool name. Set
.I fp_check_pool
to enable and
.I fp_exclude_pool
to invert.
.TP
.I fp_layout
Layout pattern (RAID0, MDT, etc.). Set
.I fp_check_layout
to enable and
.I fp_exclude_layout
to invert.
.TP
.I fp_comp_count
Component count for composite layouts. Set
.I fp_check_comp_count
to enable,
.I fp_comp_count_sign
to -1/0/1. Set
.I fp_exclude_comp_count
to invert.
.TP
.I fp_comp_flags
Component flags to match. Set
.I fp_check_comp_flags
to enable. Use
.I fp_comp_neg_flags
for flags that must not be set.
.TP
.I fp_comp_start
Component start offset. Set
.I fp_check_comp_start
to enable,
.I fp_comp_start_sign
to -1/0/1, and
.I fp_comp_start_units
for units. Set
.I fp_exclude_comp_start
to invert.
.TP
.I fp_comp_end
Component end offset. Set
.I fp_check_comp_end
to enable,
.I fp_comp_end_sign
to -1/0/1, and
.I fp_comp_end_units
for units. Set
.I fp_exclude_comp_end
to invert.
.TP
.I fp_comp_id
Component ID to match. Set
.I fp_check_comp_id
to enable and
.I fp_exclude_comp_id
to invert.
.TP
.I fp_mirror_count
Mirror count for FLR layouts. Set
.I fp_check_mirror_count
to enable,
.I fp_mirror_count_sign
to -1/0/1. Set
.I fp_exclude_mirror_count
to invert.
.TP
.I fp_mirror_state
Mirror state to match. Set
.I fp_check_mirror_state
to enable. Use
.I fp_mirror_neg_state
for states that must not be set.
.TP
.I fp_mirror_id
Mirror ID to match. Set
.I fp_check_mirror_id
to enable and
.I fp_exclude_mirror_id
to invert.
.TP
.I fp_mirror_index
Mirror index to match. Set
.I fp_check_mirror_index
to enable,
.I fp_mirror_index_sign
to -1/0/1. Set
.I fp_exclude_mirror_index
to invert.
.TP
.I fp_ext_size
Extension size for PFL layouts. Set
.I fp_check_ext_size
to enable,
.I fp_ext_size_sign
to -1/0/1, and
.I fp_ext_size_units
for units. Set
.I fp_exclude_ext_size
to invert.
.PP
.B Target Selection:
.TP
.I fp_obd_uuid
Array of OST UUIDs to match. Set
.I fp_num_obds
to the number of UUIDs. Alternatively, use
.I fp_obd_indexes
array with OST indexes. Set
.I fp_exclude_obd
to find files NOT on these OSTs.
.TP
.I fp_mdt_uuid
Array of MDT UUIDs to match. Set
.I fp_num_mdts
to the number of UUIDs. Alternatively, use
.I fp_mdt_indexes
array with MDT indexes. Set
.I fp_exclude_mdt
to find files NOT on these MDTs.
.TP
.I fp_mdt_count
MDT count for striped directories. Set
.I fp_check_mdt_count
to enable,
.I fp_mdt_count_sign
to -1/0/1. Set
.I fp_exclude_mdt_count
to invert.
.TP
.I fp_hash_type
Hash type for striped directories.
.TP
.I fp_hash_inflags
Hash flags that must be set. Set
.I fp_check_hash_flag
to enable.
.TP
.I fp_hash_exflags
Hash flags that must not be set. Set
.I fp_exclude_hash_type
to enable.
.PP
.B Extended Attributes:
.TP
.I fp_xattr_match_info
Extended attribute matching using regular expressions. Configure with
.B xattr_match_info
structure for name/value pattern matching.
.PP
.B File Attributes:
.TP
.I fp_attrs
File attributes that must be set (statx attributes). Set
.I fp_exclude_attrs
to invert.
.TP
.I fp_neg_attrs
File attributes that must not be set.
.TP
.I fp_nlink
Number of hard links. Set
.I fp_nlink_sign
to -1/0/1. Set
.I fp_exclude_nlink
to invert.
.PP
.B Foreign Files:
.TP
.I fp_foreign_type
Foreign file/directory type. Set
.I fp_check_foreign
to match foreign files and
.I fp_exclude_foreign
to exclude them.
.PP
.B Compression (if supported):
.TP
.I fp_compr_type
Compression type. Set
.I fp_check_compr_type
to enable and
.I fp_exclude_compr_type
to invert.
.TP
.I fp_compr_lvl
Compression level. Set
.I fp_check_compr_lvl
to enable,
.I fp_compr_lvl_sign
to -1/0/1. Set
.I fp_exclude_compr_lvl
to invert.
.TP
.I fp_compr_chunk
Compression chunk size. Set
.I fp_check_compr_chunk
to enable,
.I fp_compr_chunk_sign
to -1/0/1. Set
.I fp_exclude_compr_chunk
to invert.
.PP
.B Output Control:
.TP
.I fp_verbose
Verbosity level using
.B llapi_layout_verbose
enum values (VERBOSE_DEFAULT, VERBOSE_DETAIL, etc.).
.TP
.I fp_quiet
Suppress output.
.TP
.I fp_format_printf_str
Custom printf-style format string for output (similar to
.BR "lfs find --printf" ).
.TP
.I fp_yaml
Output layout information in YAML format.
.PP
.B Performance and Behavior:
.TP
.I fp_lazy
Use lazy size/block attributes when available.
.TP
.I fp_stop_on_error
Stop traversal on first error instead of continuing.
.TP
.I fp_skip_percent
Percentage of entries to skip (for sampling).
.SH RETURN VALUES
.TP
.B 0
on success.
.TP
.B <0
negative error code on failure and sets
.B errno
appropriately.
.SH ERRORS
.TP 15
.B EINVAL
Invalid arguments (e.g., path too long, invalid parameters).
.TP
.B ENOMEM
Insufficient memory for traversal or thread pool.
.TP
.B ENOENT
Starting path does not exist.
.TP
.B EACCES
Permission denied accessing files or directories.
.TP
.B ENOTDIR
Path component is not a directory.
.TP
.B EOPNOTSUPP
Operation not supported (e.g., btime on filesystems without support).
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic File Search
.EX
#include <lustre/lustreapi.h>
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>

int main(void)
{
    struct find_param param;
    int rc;

    /* Initialize to zero */
    memset(&param, 0, sizeof(param));

    /* Find all regular files larger than 1GB */
    param.fp_type = S_IFREG;
    param.fp_check_size = 1;
    param.fp_size = 1ULL << 30;  /* 1GB */
    param.fp_size_sign = 1;       /* larger than */

    rc = llapi_find("/mnt/lustre", &param);
    if (rc < 0)
        fprintf(stderr, "llapi_find failed: %s\\n",
                strerror(-rc));

    return rc;
}
.EE
.SS Search with Lustre-specific Criteria
.EX
struct find_param param;

memset(&param, 0, sizeof(param));

/* Find files with stripe count >= 4 */
param.fp_check_stripe_count = 1;
param.fp_stripe_count = 4;
param.fp_stripe_count_sign = 1;  /* >= */

/* Modified in the last 24 hours */
param.fp_mtime = time(NULL) - 86400;
param.fp_msign = 1;  /* newer than */

llapi_find("/mnt/lustre/project", &param);
.EE
.SS Parallel Traversal with Custom Callback
.EX
#include <lustre/lustreapi.h>

int my_callback(char *path, int p, int *d,
                struct find_param *param,
                struct dirent64 *de)
{
    /* Custom processing */
    printf("Found: %s\\n", path);
    return 0;  /* Continue traversal */
}

int main(void)
{
    struct find_param param;

    memset(&param, 0, sizeof(param));
    param.fp_thread_count = 8;  /* Use 8 threads */
    param.fp_max_depth = 3;     /* Max 3 levels deep */

    llapi_find_with_cb("/mnt/lustre", &param,
                       my_callback, NULL);
    return 0;
}
.EE
.SH NOTES
.IP \[bu] 2
Always initialize the
.B find_param
structure to zero before use.
.IP \[bu]
The
.I fp_thread_count
field enables parallel traversal for improved performance on large directory
trees. Set to 0 for single-threaded operation.
.IP \[bu]
When using custom callbacks with
.BR llapi_find_with_cb (),
ensure they are thread-safe if
.I fp_thread_count
> 1.
.IP \[bu]
The
.I fp_cb_data
field can pass custom data to callbacks.
.IP \[bu]
Sign fields (-1, 0, 1) indicate "less than", "equal to", or "greater than"
comparisons.
.IP \[bu]
Time comparisons use
.I fp_time_margin
for tolerance (in seconds).
.IP \[bu]
The traversal is depth-first and respects
.I fp_max_depth
and
.I fp_min_depth
boundaries.
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B llapi_find()
is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
user application interface library.
.PP
.B llapi_find_with_cb()
was added to support custom callbacks and parallel find operations.
